{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbaVbiw6kLsUPFFALJje", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "`git rebase --onto` lets you choose two things separately: the commits you move, and the new base you put them on. A plain `git rebase <upstream>` uses one argument for both.\n\n## Syntax\n\n```\ngit rebase --onto <newbase> <upstream> [<branch>]\n```\n\nThis takes the commits in `<upstream>..<branch>` (on `<branch>` but not on `<upstream>`) and replays them on top of `<newbase>`. If you leave out `<branch>`, the current branch is used.\n\n## Example: move a branch off another feature branch\n\nYou branched `feature-b` from `feature-a`, but `feature-b` doesn't depend on `feature-a`'s work and should be based on `main`:\n\n```\nmain:       A---B\n                 \\\nfeature-a:        C---D\n                       \\\nfeature-b:              E---F\n```\n\n```\ngit rebase --onto main feature-a feature-b\n```\n\nThis means: take the commits on `feature-b` that aren't on `feature-a` (E and F) and replay them onto `main`.\n\n```\nmain:       A---B\n                |\\\nfeature-a:      | C---D\n                 \\\nfeature-b:        E'---F'\n```\n\nC and D are left out. Running `git rebase main` from `feature-b` would have carried C and D along as well.\n\n## Other common uses\n\n- **Delete a range of commits:** `git rebase --onto HEAD~3 HEAD~1` drops the two commits before HEAD (`HEAD~2` and `HEAD~1`) and keeps HEAD itself.\n- **Fix a branch after its parent was rewritten:** if `feature-a` was squashed or rebased, use `git rebase --onto feature-a <old-feature-a-sha> feature-b`. This moves only `feature-b`'s own commits and doesn't replay the old versions of `feature-a`'s commits.\n\nThe replayed commits (E', F') get new SHAs. If the branch was already pushed, you'll need `git push --force-with-lease`."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7295, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11903, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7295}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "27fa5e97-44c4-4ff9-83f9-697753eb95ce", "uuid": "dcac8add-5d9d-45a0-8003-0dcb04b5680a", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:14:56.640Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbaVbNMGX7eF7e46acPw"}
